<!-- QUARRY:PART:output_schema -->
Return a JSON object with these keys:

"verdict": one of "corroborated", "not_corroborated", or "inconclusive"

"reasons": list of strings citing file/line + the observed response signal
  (accepted dangerous extension, rejection status, sanitised storage, fetch-back
  content).

"proposed_http_specs": ordered list of HTTP probe specs — the upload first, then
  its fetch-back. Each entry has: method (required), path (required), headers,
  body, multipart_fields, follow_redirects, cookies, auth_profile, vuln_class,
  functional_area. Send the file as a multipart_fields part with name, value,
  filename, and content_type; do NOT hand-roll a multipart body into `body`.
  The uploaded content must be an inert marker. Never inline creds.

"tool_calls": list of tool calls (empty when done). Each includes kind,
  tool_name, args, and reasoning (hypothesis, target_ref, expected_evidence,
  why_this_tool).

"proposed_actions": list of proposed tool actions with the same structured
  reasoning fields.

